### Rolling HMM Design

- 3 states: calm / normal / stressed

- Daily refit, full expanding window

- Leakage-free rank transform (train distribution only)

- 60 day burn-in

- Consistent relabeling by realized_vol

- Lookahead check: PASSED on all tickers

### Regime Distribution (SPY)

- Calm: 30.3% | Normal: 26.1% | Stressed: 43.6%

- Stationary distribution matches empirical — HMM internally consistent

### Transition Matrix (SPY)

- Calm persistence: 83.1% — very stable

- Normal persistence: 0.01% — transition state, not true regime

- Stressed persistence: 51.7% — moderate

### Regime Duration (SPY)

- Calm: avg 0.98 min (5.9 bars)

- Normal: avg 0.17 min (1.0 bar) — unstable

- Stressed: avg 0.35 min (2.1 bars)

### Regime Characterization (from full_characterization.csv)

| Feature      | Calm    | Normal  | Stressed |

|--------------|---------|---------|----------|

| realized_vol | 0.058   | 0.141   | 0.164    |

| spread       | 0.0179  | 0.0227  | 0.0246   |

| ofi          | 75.2    | 130.9   | 169.4    |

| queue_imb    | +0.012  | -0.009  | -0.002   |

| trade_imb    | 0.135   | 0.151   | 0.178    |

### Statistical Significance (Mann-Whitney + Cohen's d)

- 14/16 features significantly different calm vs stressed

- Large effect: realized_vol (d=1.21), microprice (d=-1.12)

- Medium effect: spread (d=0.59)

- Small effect: all OFI features (d~0.006)

- Conclusion: HMM detects VOLATILITY regimes, not OFI regimes

